  "mcp.envKeyPlaceholder": "ENV_KEY",
  "mcp.envValuePlaceholder": "value",
  "mcp.entry.stripe.summary": "Read customers, payments, subscriptions and invoices, and search Stripe's documentation.",
  "mcp.entry.stripe.containment": "The key is the boundary: one of the server's tools can call any write method of the Stripe API, so create an Agent key with read permissions only and a write is refused by Stripe rather than by a hint. Stripe also asks a person to confirm some writes, such as refunds and outbound payments, through a link. STRIPE_AUTH_HEADER takes the word Bearer, a space, then the key. It reaches mcp.stripe.com through the third-party mcp-remote bridge. If Stripe refuses the key — an empty one, or from 31 Oct 2026 one without the Agent tag — the bridge opens Stripe's sign-in in the browser instead: decline it, because that grant is your whole Stripe user and the bridge keeps it in a file on this computer, outside mcp.json.",
  "mcp.entry.notion.summary": "Search and read the pages and databases of a Notion workspace.",
  "mcp.entry.notion.containment": "It acts as you: what it reaches is decided by your permissions in the workspace you sign in to, and Notion documents no read-only switch for it, so it can edit what you can edit. Sign-in happens in the browser, so there is no key to store. It goes through the third-party mcp-remote bridge, because Notion's own local server is no longer maintained.",
  "mcp.entry.sentry.summary": "Read issues, events, traces and releases from Sentry to investigate an error.",
  "mcp.entry.sentry.containment": "Narrowed to the read-only inspect skill, which the server enforces by not registering the other tools. The token is the outer boundary: Sentry's docs ask for write scopes (project:write, team:write, event:write), so widening --skills turns those writes on. Needs Node 22.13 or newer.",
  "mcp.entry.hostinger.summary": "See and manage Hostinger VPS machines: state, backups, snapshots, firewalls and Docker.",
  "mcp.entry.hostinger.containment": "There is no read-only mode: 43 of the 64 VPS operations change something — restoring a backup or snapshot, deleting a snapshot or a firewall, stopping a container. Only the VPS group runs (billing, domains and DNS are left out), but the sign-in reaches the whole account, and the server keeps it in its own file on this machine.",
  "mcp.lastTest.ok": "last tested {when} · {n} tools",
  "mcp.lastTest.failed": "last test failed · {when}",
  "mcp.addAndTest": "Add and test",
  "mcp.addAndTest.note": "Testing starts the server's command on this computer — npx may download the package first.",
  "mcp.addAndTest.signIn": "The test may also open a sign-in page in your browser — on purpose for entries that sign in there, and for a bridge whose key is refused. It waits up to two minutes for you; if the sign-in is not finished by then, the test gives up and you can test again.",
  "mcp.secretMissing": "Paste {n} before adding: without it the server cannot sign in, and a bridge may open a browser sign-in in its place.",
  "mcp.secretFormat": "{n} is not in the form this server expects — check what the entry above says to paste. A value the service refuses can make a bridge open a browser sign-in in its place.",
