  "settings.systemOne.verify": "Verify answers grounded in sources",
  "settings.systemOne.verifyHint": "An answer written from attached documents, in a turn with no tool call, is checked by this model before it ships. If the documents don't support it, a stronger model answers and is checked again; if that fails too, the reply says the sources don't cover it.",
  "settings.systemOne.verifyMeasured": "Measured (study 26, 400 questions) with gpt-6-luna drafting: a third fewer wrong answers (33 → 21, none made worse), at about 1.9× the cost with the local verifier. Other drafting models are unmeasured. Only questions about the documents are checked; tasks (summarize, translate, rewrite…) pass straight through.",
  "settings.systemOne.verifyFallback": "If the local model isn't running: Jev (typesafe/jev-1.13) when an OpenRouter key is set, otherwise the old lexical check. A model you chose yourself has no fallback. The receipt names the verifier that ran.",
  "settings.card.bridge": "Claude",
  "settings.row.desktopBridge": "Allow Claude to operate this app",
  "settings.hint.desktopBridge": "Claude Code or Claude Desktop can read your conversations, runs and memory, and start work here, through `chimera mcp desktop`. Approvals stay with you; keys are never shared.",
  "settings.row.desktopBridgeFull": "Full control",
  "settings.hint.desktopBridgeFull": "Claude can also approve or deny actions without you and edit settings (never keys). A run Claude starts uses your models and your posture, or a narrower one, never a wider one. Which model answers and whether scheduled jobs run, Claude can only suggest, for you to approve here; granting folders, running commands, starting bots and saving agents stay yours. A prompt-injected page or message the agent reads could lead Claude to approve something.",
